---
import SponsorLayout from '@/layouts/Sponsor.astro';

const effectiveDateString: string = 'October 18, 2026';
const websiteName: string = 'Pabitra Mohan Singh';
const privacyContactEmail: string = 'support@pabitramohansingh.com';
---

<SponsorLayout title="Privacy Policy — Sponsor">
  <div class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 flex-1 relative z-10">
    
    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
        <strong>Effective date:</strong> {effectiveDateString}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
      
      <section>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">{websiteName}</strong> ("I", "me", or "my")
          handles information in connection with the sponsor page available at
          <code class="bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">/sponsor</code> and its sub-pages. It is written to be transparent,
          legally binding, and easy to read.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">1. Who is the data controller?</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller for this website is the individual open-source developer
          operating <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">{websiteName}</strong>. You can reach the controller at
          <a href={`mailto:${privacyContactEmail}`} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">{privacyContactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">2. Zero first-party data collection</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I do <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">not</strong> collect, store, or process any personal data directly
          from visitors on this sponsor page.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-2 mb-4">
          <li>No cookies are set by this website.</li>
          <li>No analytics services (such as Google Analytics) are used.</li>
          <li>No user accounts, contact forms, or comment systems are provided.</li>
          <li>No first-party tracking pixels or fingerprinting scripts are loaded.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The avatar animation on this page is a local CSS animation. It runs entirely
          in your browser and does not send any information to me or to third parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">3. Third-party sponsorship platforms</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Sponsorship is processed exclusively through <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">GitHub Sponsors</strong>
          and <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Buy Me a Coffee</strong>. When you click a sponsorship link, you
          leave this website and interact directly with those platforms.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I do not receive, store, or control your payment details, billing address,
          full name, or email address from those platforms. The platforms act as
          independent data controllers for the information they collect.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 ml-2 mb-4">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">GitHub Sponsors:</strong> GitHub may share your GitHub username,
            sponsorship tier, amount, and date with me. Payment and billing information
            are handled by GitHub and its payment processors and are not shared with me. 
            GitHub's privacy statement applies to all data it processes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Buy Me a Coffee:</strong> Buy Me a Coffee processes payments through
            PCI-compliant providers. Credit-card data is not stored on its servers. 
            Buy Me a Coffee's privacy policy governs the information it collects.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 p-4 rounded-xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
            You must refer to the privacy policies of GitHub and Buy Me a Coffee for a
            full description of their data practices and for exercising your data
            rights in relation to the information they collect.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">4. Server logs</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          This website is hosted on standard infrastructure (for example, Cloudflare or
          a comparable hosting provider). The hosting provider may automatically
          collect standard server log data, such as IP addresses, browser type,
          referring pages, and timestamps, for security, abuse prevention, and
          operational integrity.
        </p>
        <p>
          I do not use these logs to identify individual visitors, and I do not combine
          them with any other data. The hosting provider's own privacy policy governs
          its log-processing activities.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">5. Your rights under the GDPR (EEA, UK, and Switzerland)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Because this website does not collect personal data directly, the GDPR
          transparency obligations under Articles 13 and 14 are primarily satisfied by
          this notice. To the extent that any personal data is processed by
          the hosting provider or by the sponsorship platforms, you have the following
          rights:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-2 mb-4">
          <li>Right of access (Article 15 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to rectification (Article 16 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to erasure (Article 17 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to restriction of processing (Article 18 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to data portability (Article 20 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to object (Article 21 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Article 77 GDPR)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For data processed by GitHub or Buy Me a Coffee, please exercise your rights
          directly with those platforms. For any question about this website, contact
          <a href={`mailto:${privacyContactEmail}`} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">{privacyContactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">6. Your rights under the CCPA/CPRA (California)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          This website does not sell or share personal information, and it does not
          collect personal information directly from consumers. Therefore, the
          thresholds that trigger direct CCPA/CPRA obligations are not met by this
          website's first-party activities.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If you are a California resident and you interact with GitHub or Buy Me a
          Coffee, those platforms are responsible for responding to your CCPA/CPRA
          requests. You may contact them directly to exercise your rights to know,
          delete, correct, or opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal
          information.
        </p>
        <p>
          This website does not respond to Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals because
          it does not sell or share personal information and does not track visitors
          across sites.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">7. CalOPPA (California Online Privacy Protection Act)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          In accordance with CalOPPA, this Privacy Policy is publicly available and
          conspicuously linked from the sponsor page. The categories of information
          collected and the third parties with whom information may be shared are
          described above.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Do Not Track:</strong> This website does not track visitors over time
          or across third-party websites. It does not currently respond to "Do Not
          Track" browser signals because no tracking is performed.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Effective date:</strong> {effectiveDateString}. Material changes to this
          policy will be posted on this page with a new effective date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">8. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in legal
          requirements or in the services linked from this page. The effective date at
          the top of this page indicates when the latest version took effect. Continued
          use of the sponsor page after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised
          policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-3">9. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          For privacy-related questions about this website, contact:
          <a href={`mailto:${privacyContactEmail}`} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">{privacyContactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          For privacy questions about sponsorship data, please contact
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">GitHub Privacy</a>
          or
          <a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">Buy Me a Coffee Privacy</a>
          directly.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</SponsorLayout>